# Live-test credentials for duckdb-gdrive.
#
# Copy to `.env.gdrive` (gitignored, and CI-enforced by
# scripts/check_no_credentials.sh) and fill in real values.
#
# There is no fake Drive server and no HTTP replay layer in this project
# (plan decision D-1): every integration test runs against real Google Drive.
# Without these variables the live tests SKIP cleanly -- `make test` stays
# green for a developer who has no credentials. `make test_live` fails loudly
# instead, which is what CI uses.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service account (the unattended path, and what CI uses).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the service-account JSON key. Sensitive: contains an RSA private key.
GDRIVE_CI_SA_KEY_FILE=./.gcp-key.json

# In CI, pass the same key base64-encoded instead of as a file; the harness
# decodes it to a 0600 temp file at runtime and deletes it on exit.
# GDRIVE_CI_SA_KEY_B64=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The CI root the tests live in: a FOLDER in the delegated user's My Drive,
# shared with the service account as Editor (a Shared Drive id also works).
#
# The service account only reads: it has no Drive storage quota, so any upload
# it would own -- anywhere outside a Shared Drive -- returns 403 "Service
# Accounts do not have storage quota". Seeding and writes run as the delegated
# user below, who owns what it creates.
#
# See scripts/setup_ci_drive.sh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GDRIVE_CI_DRIVE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Delegated user (writes, seeding, sweeping). `make oauth_consent` fills these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GDRIVE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GDRIVE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GDRIVE_USER_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: a Shared Drive (id starts 0A) for the DRIVE_ID test,
# test/sql/gdrive_shared_drive.test.template. A Workspace USER creates it and
# adds the service account as Content manager, the delegated user as Manager. Unset,
# that test is left out with a warning (CLAUDE.md, "Known gap").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GDRIVE_CI_SHARED_DRIVE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interactive OAuth client, for the authorization_code tests (slice S-1.3).
# Type "Desktop app" in console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GDRIVE_CI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GDRIVE_CI_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: a gs:// object holding the same 100MB Parquet as the Drive
# fixture, for the REQ-NF-01 3x comparison (`make bench`).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GDRIVE_BENCH_GCS_URI=gs://datazoo-gdrive-ci/wide.parquet
